# Theme colors

All color lives in `src/assets/css/colors.css`. Components use the same Tailwind classes in light and dark. Do not use `dark:` color utilities, `bg-white`, or raw palette classes (`zinc-`, `gray-`).

- Light tokens: `:root`
- Dark tokens: `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` on `:root` (follows OS)
- Force a theme with `.light` or `.dark` on a parent (Storybook toolbar)
- New tokens: set them in `:root`, the media query, `.light`, and `.dark`, then map `--color-*` in `@theme inline`

After `npx shadcn add`, strip `dark:` color classes and point at tokens (`bg-input-background`, `border-destructive-border`, `ring-destructive-ring`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
className="bg-transparent dark:bg-input/30 aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40"

// ✅ GOOD
className="bg-input-background aria-invalid:border-destructive-border aria-invalid:ring-destructive-ring"
```
